WEBVTT

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.000
The Other House

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.510
<i>While I was hanging up the laundry,
the phone rang.</i>

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.760
<i>When I picked up the receiver,
a thin voice said, "Hello?"</i>

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.520
<i>He continued, "Is now a good time?"</i>

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.400
<i>I thought this might be that "Hey, it's me" scam
I heard on the news, so I raised my guard.</i>

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.360
<i>But then the voice said,
"It's been a while. It's Rei."</i>

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.530
Hello.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:42.580
<i>The owner of the voice was a boy who had lived
in my home up until a few years earlier.</i>

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.590
Long time no see, Tarou.
How have you been?

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.760
Tarou's become an old man, huh?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.550
Lately all he does is sleep there.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.600
Is that right, Tarou?

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.520
How is Ayumu doing?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.310
And Kyouko, too.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.280
Ayumu is going to a prep school,
and I guess you'd say Kyouko is a temp worker.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.990
She works here and there.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:23.540
<i>As I answered him, I was relieved
that he came to visit when I was alone.</i>

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:29.840
<i>If Kyouko and Ayumu were here, this living room
would have become cold in an instant.</i>

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.710
<i>Just like it did back then.</i>

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:39.680
Um, these are sweets from a shop run by
a family that's been helping me a lot lately.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.350
CRESCENT MOON

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.350
So please.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:48.980
<i>That's right. These days, in this house,
no one speaks his name anymore.</i>

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.280
I apologize for not being able
to visit in a long time.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.370
<i>"I was worried about you
since you never came by."</i>

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.540
<i>I was going to say that, but stopped myself.</i>

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.370
<i>This boy understood everything</i>

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.920
<i>and did us a favor by staying away.</i>

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.380
<i>As I awkwardly sat with him,
unable to look him in the eyes,</i>

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.130
<i>he still sat across from me.</i>

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.680
<i>So mellow...</i>

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.890
<i>That's it, mellow.</i>

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:27.810
<i>He seems much more mellow now.</i>

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.150
<i>He'd become an adult.</i>

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.900
<i>Is he the same age as Ayumu?
I can't believe it.</i>

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.910
<i>My son hasn't even changed,
and he's still a child.</i>

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:47.120
<i>I realized my children were no match for him
at a fairly early stage.</i>

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.170
<i>It was a simple situation.</i>

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.920
<i>Anyone could see that the amount
of practice he did was unbelievable.</i>

00:02:54.550 --> 00:03:00.340
<i>But if they didn't want to lose to him, they would
have to practice even more than he did.</i>

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.220
<i>It was a simple answer.</i>

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.930
<i>However, could they do it? No, they couldn't.</i>

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:12.020
<i>He silently embodied sound reasoning
and in his presence,</i>

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.070
<i>my children's own weakness
made them lose their equilibrium</i>

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.700
<i>and they collapsed into pieces.</i>

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.950
<i>When my own children
turned against me, I was lost,</i>

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.540
<i>and my husband silently watched it all unfold.</i>

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.880
<i>"People who need other people to motivate them
will eventually come up against a brick wall."</i>

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.920
<i>That was his view.</i>

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.340
<i>Unable to look at their weak selves,</i>

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.840
<i>they became caught up in enjoyments
within their reach.</i>

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:48.980
<i>One day, Ayumu declared,
"Being able to make an effort is a talent too!"</i>

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.480
<i>To those words,
my husband just chuckled, "Haha."</i>

00:03:54.190 --> 00:04:00.650
<i>I think that was the moment he gave up
on Ayumu becoming a professional shogi player.</i>

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:10.960
<i>Being around that boy, they realized that
people who wanted to reach a certain place</i>

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.130
<i>had to pursue it to that extent.</i>

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:21.170
<i>I always thought "only a small handful
of people can become what they want to be."</i>

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.300
<i>and I never thought about
what you have to do to become something.</i>

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.270
<i>And so that boy's situation
was a dreary weight on my chest.</i>

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.020
<i>And then one day,
I finally came to a realization.</i>

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:39.280
<i>That my husband
had a similar childhood as that boy.</i>

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.280
<i>I thought I understood, but I really didn't.</i>

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.160
<i>Looking past shogi,
out of all the people in the house,</i>

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:55.710
<i>the person my husband related to the most
wasn't a family member, but that boy.</i>

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.670
<i>He was wholeheartedly dedicated to shogi,</i>

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.880
<i>silently studied and did homework,</i>

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.680
<i>and even helped out around the house.</i>

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.300
<i>He really was a good boy.</i>

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.440
<i>But that made my children suffer all the more.</i>

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.980
<i>Why is he such a good boy?</i>

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.400
<i>Why didn't my children turn out like that?</i>

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.950
<i>What were the differences between the way his
mother raised him and how I raised my kids?</i>

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:31.750
<i>Did I fail in raising my children?</i>

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:37.210
<i>Or is he just playing the role of a "good boy"
as best he can since he's a freeloader?</i>

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:41.800
<i>Maybe he's laughing at us behind our backs.</i>

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.920
<i>No...</i>

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.680
<i>That's wrong.</i>

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.640
<i>He was...</i>

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.350
<i>Rei really was...</i>

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.600
<i>just a really good boy.</i>

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:01.440
<i>My children understood that, and so did I.</i>

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.360
<i>We took advantage of him.</i>

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.110
<i>We took advantage, pushed him away,
treated him shoddily,</i>

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.370
<i>and didn't give him a place to belong.</i>

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.370
<i>And so he felt like...</i>

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.870
<i>"The longer I'm around, the more strained
everyone's relations will become."</i>

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.880
<i>But he didn't even say that.</i>

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.760
<i>He just quietly left the house.</i>

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.140
<i>When the five o'clock bell rang out,
Rei got up from his chair.</i>

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:37.640
<i>He said, "Well..." and skipped
any other closing remarks,</i>

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.150
<i>apart from, "I'll come again."</i>

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:44.150
<i>"Yes, come again," I answered.</i>

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.150
<i>After all, what else could I say?</i>

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.660
See you, Tarou.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:11.890
Live a long life, okay?

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:14.560
Take care.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:25.650
<i>After Rei left, I started preparing dinner
in the kitchen.</i>

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.530
<i>As always.</i>

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:33.410
<i>Even if no one calls me, I stand here every day.</i>

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.410
<i>I make dinner and wait for everyone.</i>

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:43.790
<i>That night, I had a dream.</i>

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.300
<i>In the dream, Rei was really my son.</i>

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.680
<i>Now that he was my son,</i>

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.680
<i>Rei was sprawled out in the living room,
eating junk food, watching TV,</i>

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.810
<i>and when I told him to go to bed,
he retorted, "Oh, be quiet!"</i>

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:10.360
<i>I thought to myself,
"Well! He's the same as Ayumu and Kyouko."</i>

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:13.700
<i>I was disappointed and yet also...</i>

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.160
<i>profoundly relieved.</i>

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.960
The Other House

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:57.970
Child of March Town

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.140
<i>"Let's go to a monjayaki place."</i>

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:06.480
<i>Kiriyama invited us...</i>

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.230
<i>before Takahashi left for Kouchi.</i>

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:14.740
MONJA JIROU

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:17.030
Well, um, both of you,
congratulations on your graduation.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:22.040
And I wish you the best of luck
at the private school in Kouchi.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.210
Uh, cheer—

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.580
Wait a second.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.460
Also...

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.470
Kiriyama, congratulations
on your promotion to B-2!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.050
Thank you!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.720
C-Congratulations, Kiriyama!

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.720
JUST FOUND OUT

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.100
That's amazing!

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.100
ADMIRE

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:47.980
My grandpa was so psyched about
personally knowing a B class shogi player.

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:52.770
<i>Yes! My teacher made it to B class!</i>

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.770
He was so proud
that he couldn't contain himself.

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.990
<i>Kiriyama is a future Meijin!</i>

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.780
I appreciate that.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:03.700
I apologize for losing so quickly
at that last NHK Cup.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.040
And they were really looking forward to it.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:10.290
Aw, naw, Grandpa was like,
"Next up is the Lion King Championship!"

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.960
He's already excited about that.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.630
Thanks for waiting.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:16.800
Salmon monja and mentai mochi with cheese.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.840
- Thanks.
- Thank you!

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:25.520
Kiriyama, you're totally my grandpa's idol.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:31.650
Before he would mostly be in bed, but recently
he popped in at the neighborhood shogi club.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:37.900
SHOGI CLUB

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.780
My parents are happy too
that he's back on his feet.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.900
They're like, "Professionals are incredible!"

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.910
I want to become a professional soon, too.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.280
<i>"I want to become a professional."</i>

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:48.410
<i>Not "someday." He said "soon."</i>

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:50.790
Oh, I'll do it.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.540
- Are you sure?
- Leave it to me.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.840
<i>That's right.</i>

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:02.220
<i>In Takahashi's mind, becoming a professional
has gone from a "dream" to a "goal."</i>

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:05.560
MONJA JIROU

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:10.060
A person who helped me back in little league
is now the coach of the school in Kouchi.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:16.320
All the best players are concentrated in Tokyo,
and there are a lot of infielders.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.570
On top of that, there are dozens of schools.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:24.740
I want to raise my chances of getting
to the high school nationals, even by a little.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.460
So I decided to go where that coach is.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.590
<i>With Takahashi's practiced hands
and the clanging of the spatula,</i>

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:47.350
<i>the familiar sizzling sound
and delicious scent rose up.</i>

00:12:55.400 --> 00:13:03.280
<i>But this spring,
Takahashi will be leaving March Town.</i>

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:11.370
I wonder if they have monja in Kouchi.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:15.000
Even if they don't, I can make it.
All I need is a hot plate.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:19.090
You can get the ingredients
at any supermarket, too.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.470
Oh, I'll be bringing some sliced squid, though.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.050
I heard they're having
a welcome party at the dorm,

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.100
so I thought I'd make this as a greeting.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.020
Kind of like saying, "I'm from March Town."

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.480
<i>Ah, I see.</i>

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:39.150
<i>We're children of March Town.</i>

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:44.990
<i>No matter where we go,
that will never change.</i>

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:48.870
Yeah, that's a good idea.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:52.540
Even if they know what "monja" is,
they probably haven't tried it yet.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:56.290
Right. And I'm sure it'll be good
if Takahashi makes it.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:57.790
You bet!

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:02.340
But Grandpa told me
to at least take some spatulas for it.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:03.920
The bamboo kind to use with hot plates.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:10.310
Oh, right. They probably don't sell this
little kind there. Even if they have big ones.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.780
<i>It suddenly felt like I was going to cry.</i>

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.450
<i>He was really going to leave this place soon.</i>

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:37.420
<i>I caught myself on the verge of tears
a number of times, but I held my breath.</i>

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.290
When are you leaving?

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.000
Next week Saturday.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:45.300
That's the day of the Cherry Blossom Festival.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:48.010
Yeah. It's too bad I have to miss it.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.430
Will you do another food stand, Kawamoto?

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.970
Yeah. This time we're making
sweet red bean soup. Two kinds!

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.890
Cool. Good luck.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:58.310
Thanks.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.030
<i>This time is precious.</i>

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.910
<i>But it's flowing onward and I can't stop it.</i>

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:25.920
<i>I'm so happy that Rei invited me, giving me
the chance to talk to Takahashi a lot at the end.</i>

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.600
<i>It's great that we got to have monja together.</i>

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.810
<i>It was great.</i>

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.440
<i>And so, the morning of
the Cherry Blossom Festival came.</i>

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.690
CRESCENT MOON

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.690
SWEET RED BEAN SOUP
AZUKI
WALNUT

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:47.940
TEA

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:52.570
All right, preparations complete!

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.200
Shall we get started?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.620
Welcome!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:04.210
Who would like some
sweet red bean soup with rice dumplings?

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:10.430
Oh, Crescent Moon is serving up
tasty food again.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.090
It's thick, sweet, and salty.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:16.600
Good to hear! It has light-brown miso inside.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.560
This warms me up.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.810
It's still chilly by the riverside.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:23.980
Oh, then I'll have
some sweet red bean soup with walnuts.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.230
HEAVY

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:32.240
Tupperware containing
the cash made from sales

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.150
Yes, business is booming!

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:32.240
It's still cold outside, so going with
something warm was the right choice!

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.870
How's it going?!

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.450
If you start running low
on dumplings, let me know!

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:38.200
MERCHANT

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:38.200
I'll boil up as many as we need!

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:42.250
If that happens, you call out the secret phrase,
"Brown sugar syrup roasted soy flour!"

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.710
- Got it!
- Roger!

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.050
Are you sure you don't want to see him off?

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.300
MILK TAKAHASHI

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.270
No. That's okay.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:45.980
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.320
Hup!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.200
<i>Takahashi. I'm going to do my best here, too.</i>

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:57.780
Excuse me! Two soups with walnuts, please!

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.660
Okay! Coming right up!

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.460
What? Hina cut her hair?

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.420
That's a major event in a young girl's life!

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:12.460
Oh. Did she cut her hair
because a crush was quashed?

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.800
That's right! She suddenly told me last night!

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.720
It's so bittersweet!

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.850
Sis, I'm thinking of getting a haircut.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.480
Huh? S-Sure, why not?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.360
Is this that legendary...

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.910
<i>I will cut my hair</i>

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:44.000
<i>to give a proper send-off to my childhood self</i>

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:48.920
<i>and to take a step forward as the new me.</i>

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:52.840
I could tell she was reading
that kind of poem in her head!

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:56.470
How can I put it? I'm at a loss!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.260
Oh, geez!

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.720
My little sister is too cute!

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.720
This is the springtime of her life!

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:05.980
Hina! It's so bittersweet!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:10.060
Akari, don't you dare
say any of that to Hina.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:10.060
UMM...

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.730
I'm sure she would faint
out of embarrassment.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:16.490
I'm home.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:19.490
Hina! How'd it go?

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:20.490
At the beauty salon...

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:23.120
GLOOM

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.120
EHH!?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.120
Huh? What's wrong?

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:28.540
It was a failure.
I'm never leaving the house again.

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:31.380
I'll go to high school
from the second semester.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.380
H-Here, let me take a look.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:37.630
O-Oh, Hina.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.880
I-It looks great!

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.510
Yeah.

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:43.220
How should I say it.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:47.640
It's a very middle school look...

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:49.390
SHIVER
SHIVER

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.390
No! I mean...

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:51.980
I mean such a high school look...

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:51.980
TINY

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:56.150
Uh, a-anyway,
it looks really good on you! Yes!

00:19:56.610 --> 00:20:01.070
I-I asked her to give me an adult-like bob...

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.910
B-But only an old woman was at the salon...

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.410
Oh, Hina! A bob?

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.540
Okay, you can count on me.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.790
THE NEXT DAY

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:16.130
Oof...

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:17.630
What the hell?!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:20.760
Oh, Hina? I thought it was a household deity!

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:20.760
HA-WHA?

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.510
Hey, Grandpa!

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.510
YOU CAN'T
SAY THAT!!

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.640
Hina! Here!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:25.890
I'm not a kokeshi doll!

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.140
Momo, how could you!

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.140
NOOO

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.140
Apparently trying
to cheer her up

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:30.640
- Hina, here! Hina!
- I'm never going outside!

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.150
I'll become a shut-in!

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.770
I can't hold it in any longer!

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.530
Please, Hina!
Hold this just for a second!

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:38.530
CANDY DROPS

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.360
- You too, Sis?!
- Come on, please?

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:44.030
- Please, just for a little bit!
- No!

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:46.280
- Oh please, Hina?
- Hina!

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:47.040
Child of March Town

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:21.460
Hina, Kiriyama has come to pick you up.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:26.510
Hey! If you don't come out,
Kiriyama is going to be late, too.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:33.680
Hina, just resign yourself to it and come out.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.510
STARE

00:23:07.510 --> 00:23:10.930
I-It's weird, isn't it?
I-I never should've done it.

00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:13.310
It looks stupid, doesn't it?!

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:13.310
HAWAWA

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:16.430
I really do look like that household deity
with the bowl hairstyle!

00:23:15.980 --> 00:23:18.190
WAHHH

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:19.850
Yeah, it's nice.

00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:24.320
Huh?

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:25.820
Yeah, it's nice.

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:27.070
Yeah, yeah.

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:28.820
It's really nice.

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:32.580
Rei?

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:35.450
Yeah, something about it. I really like it!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.790
What? Um...

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:39.460
It totally suits you!

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:45.460
U-Um... thank you...

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:06.740
Yeah, yeah.

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:08.990
E-Enough already!

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:10.200
I like it!

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:12.030
You're embarrassing me!

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:13.660
I think it's great!

00:24:13.660 --> 00:24:16.080
Just stop it!

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:45.020
ILLUSTRATION:
CHIKA UMINO

00:24:31.090 --> 00:24:33.800
Thank you for watching...

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:36.100
March comes in like a lion!

00:24:36.100 --> 00:24:37.970
Let's meet again!

00:24:37.970 --> 00:24:39.730
Bye-bye!
